    "long_instructions": "#### A computer system is a set of parts that work together to process information and complete tasks. Simply put, it includes:\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 10px; padding: 15px; margin: 20px auto; max-width: 85%; box-sizing: border-box; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;\">📖 <strong>Hardware</strong> the physical parts.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;\">📖 <strong>Software</strong> the programs that run on it.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;\">📖 <strong>Operating System</strong> manages the hardware and software.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n>#### 📝 Watch this video and consider:\r\n>- #### How the different parts of a computer system — **hardware, software, and the operating system** — work together."
  },
